# Normalise line endings to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This package is authored on Windows and released from a Linux CI runner. Without
# this, the first commit stores CRLF, the runner checks out CRLF, and every
# subsequent sync of an otherwise-identical tree shows every file as modified —
# which makes the release diff, the one artifact a human is expected to read in
# full before publishing, completely unreadable.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than bare `text=auto` so checkouts are LF too, on every
# platform. Nothing here is sensitive to native line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish artefacts: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
